## Why This Is Asked
Assess ability to quantify economics of on-device ML features, balancing privacy, latency, and cloud savings at scale across enterprises.

## Key Concepts
- On-device indexing and embeddings
- Energy budgets and edge compute
- Delta-sync and privacy-compliant telemetry
- Multi-tenant rollout and org-level scaling
- Regulatory/compliance costs and go/no-go criteria

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simple relevant cash-flow function for CBA
function cbaNPV(cf, r) {
  let npv = 0;
  for (let t = 0; t < cf.length; t++) {
    npv += cf[t] / Math.pow(1 + r, t + 1);
  }
  return npv;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate the energy model across devices with different hardware?
- How would you quantify productivity uplift from improved search latency in organizations?

## Why This Is Asked
This probes a candidate's ability to quantify costs for an on-device feature with privacy constraints and optional cloud lifts, focusing on edge-cases and governance.

## Key Concepts
- On-device storage budgeting
- Edge compute energy budget
- Privacy/compliance & consent overhead
- Rollout strategy and drift maintenance

## Code Example
```javascript
function estimateAnnualCost(storageMB, cpuW, users, cloudPerUser) {
  const storageCost = storageMB * 0.01;
  const energyCost = cpuW * 24 * 365 * 0.0003;
  const telemetry = users * cloudPerUser;
  return storageCost + energyCost + telemetry;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate the break-even horizon with real usage data?
- What safeguards would you implement for data minimization and consent revocation?

